      {
        "Id": "04f890b612064ce8be5487f6e060757f",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE  -  link the CAD and / or draw the door swing with Revit lines (arc), Run\nEvery swing arc next to a wall becomes a door in that wall at the same place: width = CAD width, height = 2100 (your setting), same hinge + swing.\nTwo leaves meeting in the middle = DOUBLE door.  Types A_DR_SGL_0900x2100 / A_DR_DBL_1500x2100.  Existing doors are kept; script doors are updated.\nSelection mode: pick walls (doors only in them), door lines (only those), or doors (set their height).  Run again any time - never doubled.",
        "DescriptionText": null,
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
        "Nodes": [],
        "HasNestedGroups": false,
        "Left": 0.0,
        "Top": -330.0,
        "Width": 0.0,
